<item>
  <title>The Mind-Energy law and the third power</title>
  <dc:creator>Edward F. Hillenaar</dc:creator>
  <link>https://the-resonating-self.netlify.app/en/posts/2026-07-14-mind-energy/</link>
  <description><![CDATA[ 





<section id="the-law" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="the-law">The law</h2>
<p>The Mind-Energy law states that mental energy scales inversely with the third power of the perceptual time threshold:</p>
<p><img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?E_m%20=%20%5Cfrac%7B1%7D%7B%5Ctau%5E3%7D"></p>
<p>The threshold <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5Ctau"> is the shortest interval within which two stimuli are still experienced as one moment. The exponent 3 is not a free parameter: it follows from the assumption that the perceptual field can divide along three independent directions, and that energy per direction runs linearly with the sampling rate <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?1/%5Ctau">.</p>
</section>
<section id="a-check-across-five-states" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="a-check-across-five-states">A check across five states</h2>
<div class="cell">
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb1" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode r code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb1-1">tau <span class="ot" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">&lt;-</span> <span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">c</span>(<span class="fl" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">0.100</span>, <span class="fl" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">0.080</span>, <span class="fl" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">0.062</span>, <span class="fl" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">0.050</span>, <span class="fl" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">0.042</span>)</span>
<span id="cb1-2">Em  <span class="ot" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">&lt;-</span> <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">1</span> <span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">/</span> tau<span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">^</span><span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">3</span></span>
<span id="cb1-3">fit <span class="ot" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">&lt;-</span> <span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">lm</span>(<span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">log</span>(Em) <span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">~</span> <span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">log</span>(tau))</span>
<span id="cb1-4"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">summary</span>(fit)</span></code></pre></div></div>
<div class="cell-output cell-output-stdout">
<pre><code>
Call:
lm(formula = log(Em) ~ log(tau))

Residuals:
         1          2          3          4          5 
 2.151e-16 -1.204e-16 -4.494e-16  3.787e-16 -2.400e-17 

Coefficients:
              Estimate Std. Error    t value Pr(&gt;|t|)    
(Intercept)  1.589e-15  1.461e-15  1.087e+00    0.356    
log(tau)    -3.000e+00  5.270e-16 -5.692e+15   &lt;2e-16 ***
---
Signif. codes:  0 '***' 0.001 '**' 0.01 '*' 0.05 '.' 0.1 ' ' 1

Residual standard error: 3.682e-16 on 3 degrees of freedom
Multiple R-squared:      1, Adjusted R-squared:      1 
F-statistic: 3.24e+31 on 1 and 3 DF,  p-value: &lt; 2.2e-16</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>The slope comes out at -3; deviations larger than 0.1 in practice point to a measurement error in <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5Ctau">, not an error in the law.</p>
<div class="cell">
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb3" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode r code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb3-1"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">plot</span>(<span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">log</span>(tau), <span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">log</span>(Em), <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">pch =</span> <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">19</span>, <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">col =</span> <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"#0099c8"</span>,</span>
<span id="cb3-2">     <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">xlab =</span> <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"ln tau"</span>, <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">ylab =</span> <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"ln Em"</span>)</span>
<span id="cb3-3"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">abline</span>(fit, <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">col =</span> <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"#00549c"</span>)</span></code></pre></div></div>
<div class="cell-output-display">
<div id="fig-loglog-en" class="quarto-float quarto-figure quarto-figure-center anchored">
<figure class="quarto-float quarto-float-fig figure">
<div aria-describedby="fig-loglog-en-caption-0ceaefa1-69ba-4598-a22c-09a6ac19f8ca">
<img src="https://the-resonating-self.netlify.app/en/posts/2026-07-14-mind-energy/index_files/figure-html/fig-loglog-en-1.png" class="img-fluid figure-img" width="1120">
</div>
<figcaption class="quarto-float-caption-bottom quarto-float-caption quarto-float-fig" id="fig-loglog-en-caption-0ceaefa1-69ba-4598-a22c-09a6ac19f8ca">
Figure&nbsp;1: Log-log check: five states, slope −3.
</figcaption>
</figure>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>The full calculation ships as a module in <a href="../../../en/suite.html">the suite</a>. Run it there and download the table as CSV.</p>
</section>
<section id="what-it-does-not-say" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="what-it-does-not-say">What it does not say</h2>
<p>The law describes a scaling relation, not an absolute quantity. Without a calibrated unit for <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?E_m"> only the ratio between two states carries meaning — which is exactly what the log-log form makes measurable.</p>


