<item>
  <title>From .qmd to published article</title>
  <dc:creator>Edward F. Hillenaar</dc:creator>
  <link>https://the-resonating-self.netlify.app/en/posts/2026-01-19-quarto-workflow/</link>
  <description><![CDATA[ 





<section id="four-steps" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="four-steps">Four steps</h2>
<ol type="1">
<li><strong>Write.</strong> New article: <code>en/posts/YYYY-MM-DD-slug/index.qmd</code>. The YAML header carries title, <code>description</code>, <code>date</code>, <code>categories</code> and <code>image</code>. The prose is markdown; calculations sit in R chunks.</li>
<li><strong>Render.</strong> In RStudio: <strong>Build → Render Website</strong>, or <code>quarto render</code> in the terminal. The result lands in <code>_site/</code>, including the figures the R chunks drew.</li>
<li><strong>Push.</strong> Source and <code>_site/</code> go to GitHub in one commit.</li>
<li><strong>Publish.</strong> Netlify picks up <code>_site</code> and puts the new version live. No build step on the server.</li>
</ol>
</section>
<section id="why-rendered-html-is-committed" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="why-rendered-html-is-committed">Why rendered HTML is committed</h2>
<p>Because the R chunks need packages and data that need not live on a build server. Rendering locally keeps output reproducible on one machine and the deploy simple: Netlify publishes what is there.</p>
<p><code>freeze: auto</code> in <code>_quarto.yml</code> makes a chunk re-run only when its <code>.qmd</code> file changed. The stored results live in <code>_freeze/</code> and are committed too.</p>
</section>
<section id="draft-and-publication" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="draft-and-publication">Draft and publication</h2>
<p>Set <code>draft: true</code> in the YAML header and the article stays out of the listing. Half-finished pieces sit safely in the repository without going live.</p>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode" id="cb1" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode yaml code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode yaml"><span id="cb1-1"><span class="pp" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">---</span></span>
<span id="cb1-2"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">title</span><span class="kw" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-weight: bold;
font-style: inherit;">:</span><span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"> </span><span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"Working title"</span></span>
<span id="cb1-3"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">date</span><span class="kw" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-weight: bold;
font-style: inherit;">:</span><span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"> 2026-09-01</span></span>
<span id="cb1-4"><span class="fu" style="color: #4758AB;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">draft</span><span class="kw" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-weight: bold;
font-style: inherit;">:</span><span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"> </span><span class="ch" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">true</span></span>
<span id="cb1-5"><span class="pp" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">---</span></span></code></pre></div></div>


